From: Inga Pilchin <inga.pilchin@realsenseai.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] realsense: media-bus codes for H.264 and JPEG over the 8-bit carrier

H.264 and JPEG ride the same opaque 8-bit CSI carrier as the variable-length
row added by the previous patch. Each keeps a private code, so the capture
node offers them as distinct, selectable formats and the carrier rows never
match another sensor's standard H.264 or JPEG code. Both use standard pixel
formats.

Signed-off-by: Inga Pilchin <inga.pilchin@realsenseai.com>
---
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
index 2e03e14bbc60..4db3bce0d1a5 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
@@ -179,6 +179,11 @@
  * up to the declared height, over an opaque 8-bit CSI carrier */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RS_VARLEN_1X8		0x500a
 
+/* RealSense H.264 and JPEG over the opaque 8-bit carrier: own codes, so the
+ * carrier rows never match another sensor's standard H.264 or JPEG code. */
+#define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RS_H264_1X8		0x500b
+#define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RS_JPEG_1X8		0x500c
+
 /* HSV - next is	0x6002 */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_AHSV8888_1X32		0x6001
 
